**Claim 1**

A compound represented by the following formula (1):

**[Formula (1)]**

R¹—[A(R²)ₘ₂(R³)ₘ₃]ₙ—[B(R⁴)ₘ₄(R⁵)ₘ₅]—R⁵

wherein, in the formula (1):

R¹ represents a hydrogen atom, a halogen atom, a hydroxyl group, a substituted or unsubstituted alkyl group having 1 to 20 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted alkoxy group having 1 to 20 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted aryl group having 6 to 30 carbon atoms, or a substituted or unsubstituted heteroaryl group having 3 to 30 ring atoms;

R² and R³ each independently represent a hydrogen atom, a halogen atom, a cyano group, a nitro group, a substituted or unsubstituted alkyl group having 1 to 20 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted cycloalkyl group having 3 to 20 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted alkoxy group having 1 to 20 carbon atoms, or a substituted or unsubstituted aryl group having 6 to 30 carbon atoms;

R⁴ and R⁵ each independently represent a hydrogen atom, a halogen atom, a substituted or unsubstituted alkyl group having 1 to 20 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted alkenyl group having 2 to 20 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted aryl group having 6 to 30 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted heteroaryl group having 3 to 30 ring atoms, or a substituted or unsubstituted amino group;

wherein, when a plurality of each of R² to R⁵ is present, the plurality thereof may be the same as or different from one another, and adjacent groups selected from R² to R⁵ may be bonded to each other to form a substituted or unsubstituted ring;

m2, m3, m4, and m5 each independently represent an integer of 0 to 4;

n represents an integer of 1 to 3; and

p2, p3, p4, and p5 each independently represent an integer of 0 to 5,

with the proviso that at least one of m2 to m5 is 1 or more.

# Claim 1

**1.** A vinylphenylmethyl-containing polyfunctional compound represented by the following General Formula (I):

**[Chemical Formula I]**

$$\left[ \mathrm{CH_2{=}CH{-}Ar{-}CH_2} \right]_{n} {-} Z {-} \left[ R^1 \right]_{m}$$

wherein:

**Ar** represents a phenylene group selected from the group consisting of an *ortho*-phenylene group, a *meta*-phenylene group, and a *para*-phenylene group, wherein the phenylene group is optionally substituted with from 1 to 4 substituents each independently selected from the group consisting of a C₁–C₆ alkyl group, a C₁–C₆ alkoxy group, a halogen atom, a hydroxyl group, and a nitro group;

**Z** represents an (n+m)-valent linking group selected from the group consisting of:
- (a) a single bond (only when n + m = 2),
- (b) a substituted or unsubstituted C₁–C₃₀ aliphatic hydrocarbon group, which optionally contains one or more heteroatoms selected from oxygen, nitrogen, sulfur, silicon, and phosphorus,
- (c) a substituted or unsubstituted C₆–C₃₀ aromatic hydrocarbon group,
- (d) a heterocyclic group having from 3 to 30 ring atoms and containing at least one heteroatom selected from oxygen, nitrogen, and sulfur, and
- (e) a linking group comprising a combination of two or more of the groups defined in (b), (c), and (d), optionally joined through one or more divalent connecting moieties selected from –O–, –S–, –C(=O)–, –C(=O)O–, –OC(=O)O–, –NR²–, –C(=O)NR²–, –SO₂–, –Si(R³)₂–, and –O–Si(R³)₂–O–;

**R¹**, when present, represents at each occurrence independently a functional group selected from the group consisting of a hydroxyl group, a carboxyl group, an amino group, an epoxy group, a glycidyloxy group, an isocyanato group, a (meth)acryloyloxy group, a vinyl group, an allyl group, a mercapto group, a halogen atom, an alkoxysilyl group, a cyano group, and a C₁–C₁₀ alkyl group substituted with any one of the foregoing functional groups;

**R²** represents a hydrogen atom or a C₁–C₆ alkyl group;

**R³** represents at each occurrence independently a C₁–C₆ alkyl group or a phenyl group;

**n** represents an integer of from 1 to 6; and

**m** represents an integer of from 0 to 6;

with the proviso that:

(i) the sum of **n** and **m** is an integer of from 2 to 8;

(ii) at least one vinylphenylmethyl moiety, –CH₂–Ar–CH=CH₂, is bonded to **Z** through the methylene (–CH₂–) carbon thereof; and

(iii) when **Z** represents a single bond, then **n** is 1, **m** is 1, and **R¹** is other than a hydrogen atom.
